## Claim
Text: "Viral video purportedly shows Pakistani opposition MPs chanted ‘Modi, Modi’ (India's PM)  inside the Pakistani Parliament"
Claim author: BJP MP Shobha Karandlaje
Claim date: October 28, 2020
Claim origin: https://web.archive.org/web/20201029052913/https://twitter.com/ShobhaBJP/status/1321685388029689857

## Initial Q&A
### 1. Does a viral video exist that was shared by BJP MP Shobha Karandlaje on Twitter on or around October 28, 2020, claiming to show Pakistani opposition MPs chanting "Modi, Modi" inside the Pakistani Parliament?
Answer: **Yes**, a viral video was shared by BJP leaders, including MP Shobha Karandlaje, on Twitter around October 28, 2020, claiming to show Pakistani opposition MPs chanting "Modi, Modi" inside the Pakistani Parliament. The Alt News article specifically lists "Sobha Karandlaje" among the BJP leaders who promoted this claim. However, the fact-check revealed that the video was misrepresented — the slogans heard in the Pakistani National Assembly were actually "voting-voting," not "Modi-Modi," and India TV's broadcast on October 28, 2020 distorted the sequence of events. The viral video continued to be shared by various BJP figures and media outlets in subsequent months.

